I don't know all the nuances and pitfalls off the top of my head [I've
never needed to do it], but a confused b?remove curse can be used to
create (un)holy water without resorting to prayer.  Do you have a bunch
of useless potions that can be blanked?

IIRC, human (or elven, if you are an elf) sacrifice *never* results in
a positive outcome.  For non-chaotics, the altar becomes chaotic, your
god is irritated, and other bad things happen (so don't do that :-).
Chaotics summon a peaceful demon, but get no other benefit.

> So, here I stand in front of the lawful temple.  Is there anything that
> I can do to appease Huan Ti?  What happens if I sacrifice a lawful
> priest on a lawful altar?  Or am I better off keeping my poly rings on
> and descending to a chaotic altar a bit further down and waiting for a
> decent sacrifice?

Your god is angry with you.  Unless you can afford to change alignment,
don't mess about with cross-aligned altars.  You will convert yourself.
On the flip side, non-chaotic gods are easier to appease by sacrifice
than chaotic ones.  I'd probably head back down to the deepest chaotic
altar you can find.

Other things you might consider:
1. Make some holy water via confused b?r.curse, bless a lamp, then
   wish for the corpse of a suitable sacrifice.
2. Reverse genocide something suitable.
3. Stick with the rings of poly/poly control and do without prayer the
   rest of the way.

